+`.env` uses the usual dotenv syntax: `KEY=value`, optional single or double quotes around the value, an optional leading `export `, and `#` comment lines. An unquoted value may end with a ` # comment` (a space before the `#`); inside quotes the `#` is kept as part of the value. A UTF-8 byte order mark at the start of the file is ignored.
+
+## Diagnosing configuration
+
+Run `python -m payhook doctor` to print every setting, its effective value and where that value came from (`environment`, `.env` or `default`). Secrets (`PAYHOOK_API_TOKEN`, `PAYHOOK_WEBHOOK_SECRET`) are shown only as their length, and any username or password in `PAYHOOK_ENDPOINT` is hidden. The output is safe to paste into a support ticket. `doctor` always exits with 0; missing required settings are listed in its last line.
+
+`python -m payhook check` prints `ok`, or the names of missing settings, and exits non-zero if any are missing.
 
 Run the tests with `python -m unittest`.
