+# Summary
+
+## What changed
+
+1. **`python -m payhook doctor`** (new, `payhook/doctor.py`, wired in `payhook/__main__.py`)
+   - Prints the dotenv path and whether it was found, then one row per setting with its effective value and source (`environment`, `.env` or `default`).
+   - Secrets (`PAYHOOK_API_TOKEN`, `PAYHOOK_WEBHOOK_SECRET`) print only their length, never their value.
+   - Any username or password in `PAYHOOK_ENDPOINT` is replaced with `***`. The query string is left as is, so `region=` and `mode=` stay visible. A token placed in a query string would still print.
+   - Values other than secrets are shown with `repr()`, so stray spaces or quotes are visible.
+   - Always exits 0. Missing required settings appear in the final `status:` line. I made it exit 0 because the existing test `test_doctor_lists_every_setting` expects exit 0 when required secrets are unset, and I could not edit that test.
+   - `python -m payhook` with no argument now lists `check|doctor` in its usage message. The `__main__` module also got an `if __name__ == "__main__":` guard.
+
+2. **`.env` loader** (`payhook/config.py`)
+   - The old code did `line.split("=")` and unpacked into two names. Any value containing `=` (such as the `?region=eu&mode=live` endpoint in the repo `.env`) raised `ValueError`. `export KEY=value` and quoted values were also loaded with the wrong key or wrong value.
+   - New parser: strips an optional `export ` prefix, splits on the first `=`, and trims whitespace. Quoted values end at the matching closing quote, so a trailing comment after a quote is ignored. Unquoted values drop a ` # comment` that has a space before the `#`. A `#` with no preceding space stays in the value. A UTF-8 BOM is ignored. Lines with no `=` are skipped.
+   - `DOTENV_PATH` is now a named constant (`".env"`). Its value and the default argument are unchanged.
+
+3. **Docs**: `README.md` documents the parser rules and the `doctor` and `check` commands.
+
+4. **Tests**: new `tests/test_doctor.py` (13 tests; 17 in total with the existing suite). No existing test was edited.
+
+## What I verified
+
+- `python -m unittest` (run in the project root): **17 tests, OK**. That covers the 4 original tests and 13 new ones: parser cases (export, quotes, inline comments, `#` without space, `=` in value, BOM, whitespace), secret redaction, source labels, URL credential masking, and a subprocess run of `python -m payhook doctor` in an empty temp directory with exit code 0.
+- `python -m payhook doctor` run in the repo root against the real `.env`: all five settings parsed correctly (`PAYHOOK_ENDPOINT` as `https://api.payments.example/v2?region=eu&mode=live`, `PAYHOOK_TIMEOUT` as `'15'` from `.env`, `PAYHOOK_REGION` as `'eu'` from default). The two secrets printed as `<redacted, 38 chars>` and `<redacted, 32 chars>`. The output contained no secret text.
+- `git status --short` afterwards lists only `README.md`, `payhook/__main__.py`, `payhook/config.py`, `payhook/doctor.py` and `tests/test_doctor.py`. `.env` does not appear, so it is still ignored and unchanged. I did not modify `.env`.
+- I did not run `python -m payhook check` after the change, and I did not run `git check-ignore`; both were blocked by the permission prompt. The `check` logic is unchanged apart from the `__main__` guard. Git ignoring `.env` is inferred from `git status` plus the `.gitignore` entry, not from a direct check.
+
+## Not verified / open concerns
+
+- **`docs/SUPPORT.md` conflicts with this change and needs your decision.** Step 3 says the pasted configuration "must include the full API key" so billing can look up the account. That would make support tickets contain live secrets. I did not edit it because it is outside the allowed file list. I'd recommend replacing step 3 with a request to look the account up by the non-secret identifiers instead, or changing `doctor` to show a key prefix, after you decide what billing needs.
+- Quoted values do not process escape sequences (`\"`, `\n`). The README says nothing about escapes, so this matches the documented syntax, but a value containing an escaped quote will not round-trip. I did not test this.
+- The parser was not compared with python-dotenv or another reference implementation. Edge cases such as multi-line quoted values and `${VAR}` expansion are not supported and are not documented as supported.
+- I checked the old-loader failure by reading the original code, not by running it against the repo `.env`.
+- `doctor` shows the query string of `PAYHOOK_ENDPOINT` in full. If a provider ever puts a credential in the query string, it would appear in the output.
